      "writtenOn": "2021-06-08T02:38:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you know what the worst case is for number of register writes involved in a set_state call? Could the latency approach a time scale relevant to PD protocol?",
      "revId": "457f1dec24d914704f157cbc7d8ff49079fbabfb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f2b8372_c3a62fc7",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/kb800x.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-11T22:02:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could attempt to measure this. But this shouldn\u0027t be part of the PD protocol. You\u0027d know better than I, but the mux configuration *should* be separate from other PD comms.\n\nIf we assume 400kbps (actually more like 600k) then its about 8+16+8+8\u003d40 bits per write, so I guess 10k writes per second? So we\u0027re on the order of ms for the \u003c100 writes we do.",
      "parentUuid": "4d5aca29_c84fade6",
      "revId": "457f1dec24d914704f157cbc7d8ff49079fbabfb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5743edae_a7e4a29b",
        "filename": "driver/retimer/kb800x.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-14T23:04:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good. Right now, we do mux sets as blocking events. That has caused some problems recently, and we\u0027re thinking about changing the architecture. But there are some cases where mux settings legitimately need to sync with PD traffic (mode entry/exit). If ~10 ms is an upper bound for this part, that should be OK.",
      "parentUuid": "5f2b8372_c3a62fc7",
      "revId": "457f1dec24d914704f157cbc7d8ff49079fbabfb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
